<td id="S3.T1.1.4.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.7pt 10.0pt;"><math id="S3.T1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1456{\pm}0.0000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.1456</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">±</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.0000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1456{\pm}0.0000</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="S3.T1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_parbox ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:345.0pt;"><span id="S3.T1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">“F1@thr” uses the validation PR-curve maximum with <math id="S3.T1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. ECE and F1 are undefined for the always-negative baseline (shown as “—”).</span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Analysis (classification).</span>
Under matched budgets and strict causality, GRU-D slightly exceeds the Transformer in discrimination and proper scoring on MIT–BIH (AUROC <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.92" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.92</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.92</annotation></semantics></math> vs. <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.89" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.89</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.89</annotation></semantics></math>, higher AUPRC, lower Brier), while both achieve similar F<sub id="S3.p5.1.2" class="ltx_sub">2</sub>-tuned F1 near <math id="S3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.59" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.59</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.59</annotation></semantics></math>. Despite temperature scaling, ECE remains nontrivial (<math id="S3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 0.27" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.27</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 0.27</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.30</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.30</annotation></semantics></math>), underscoring the importance of calibration when translating probabilities into alerts. Grouped bootstraps show wide record-to-record variability, which we report per-seed in the supplement.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE II: </span>Task 3: One-step HR forecasting (bpm) after a 60 s context. Mean<math id="S3.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math>std over seeds. Metrics are computed in original units after inverse normalizing.</figcaption>
<div id="S3.T2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:47.4pt;vertical-align:-21.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-6.4pt,0.9pt) scale(0.964284293169222,0.964284293169222) ;">
<table id="S3.T2.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S3.T2.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
